# Shell scripts MUST be stored and checked out with LF, always.
#
# This machine has core.autocrlf=true, so every .sh in this repo was being
# committed with CRLF. Git Bash on Windows tolerates that, which is why it went
# unnoticed for months; real Linux does not. A CRLF shebang makes the kernel
# look for an interpreter literally named "bash\r" and the script dies with
# "bad interpreter: No such file or directory". Sourced from .bashrc instead,
# the \r becomes part of every token and you get syntax errors on lines that
# look perfectly fine.
#
# claudecm-linux.sh is the module the Linux box actually runs. Do not let this
# regress.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf

# PowerShell is Windows-side and CRLF is correct for it.
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.psd1  text eol=crlf

# Documents and config: normalise in the repo, let the platform decide locally.
*.md    text
*.json  text
*.txt   text
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitignore     text eol=lf
